From 0e0944d4215127dc3b5e3245484bd57490556f57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:57:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] grate: implement fragment max()

TGSI MAX (0x0d) was refused by the fragment compiler, which blocked
almost every three.js and glmark2 lighting shader (saturate(), clamp(),
max(dot(n, l), 0.0)). The ALU already has the MAX op (2), next to MIN
(1), so add MAX to the same code path as MIN: ALU op MAX, the second
value in the third source (with it in the second one the op returns
min/max(a * b, 0)), and the same operand staging and scalarization
for spilling.

Checked three ways. Against a CPU model on the tablet: six new cases of
grate-frag-compare-test (max of two uniforms, of a varying and a
uniform, of two varyings, of negated values, against a literal zero, and
min(max()) together) pass, as do the 13 older ones. Against NVIDIA's
compiler (the Android one on the tablet, decoded with ar20bin-dump.py):
max(c.rgb, 0.5), max of two lanes of one sample and max(c, uniform) all
come out as ALU op 2 with the value in A, the constant one in B and the
other value in C, the layout of min() with op 1. And glmark2 now runs
the blinn-phong-inf and bump tests that stopped at 0x0d.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/tgsi.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/tgsi.c b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/tgsi.c
index 0dc9fa7dfdd..226b7dc85b0 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/tgsi.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/fp/tgsi.c
@@ -631,9 +631,10 @@ emit_vALU(struct grate_fp_shader *fp, const struct tgsi_dst_register *dst,
          op.src[2] = fp_tgsi_src(fp, third, i, mfu);
          break;
       case TGSI_OPCODE_MIN:
+      case TGSI_OPCODE_MAX:
          /* like ADD, the second value is the third source: with it in the
           * second one the op returned min(a * b, 0) (measured) */
-         op.op = FP_ALU_OP_MIN;
+         op.op = opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_MIN ? FP_ALU_OP_MIN : FP_ALU_OP_MAX;
          op.src[1] = fp_alu_src_one();
          op.src[2] = b;
          break;
@@ -1218,6 +1219,7 @@ emit_tgsi_instr(struct grate_fp_shader *fp, const struct tgsi_full_instruction *
    case TGSI_OPCODE_SGE:
    case TGSI_OPCODE_SEQ:
    case TGSI_OPCODE_MIN:
+   case TGSI_OPCODE_MAX:
    case TGSI_OPCODE_MUL: {
       const struct tgsi_src_register *a = &inst->Src[0].Register;
       const struct tgsi_src_register *b = &inst->Src[1].Register;
@@ -1848,6 +1850,7 @@ scalarize_for_spilling(struct util_dynarray *instructions)
       case TGSI_OPCODE_ADD:
       case TGSI_OPCODE_MUL:
       case TGSI_OPCODE_MIN:
+      case TGSI_OPCODE_MAX:
       case TGSI_OPCODE_SLT:
       case TGSI_OPCODE_SGE:
       case TGSI_OPCODE_SEQ:
